{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "title": "ProxyOmega Reseller API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "## Overview\nThe ProxyOmega Reseller API allows you to programmatically manage sub-accounts, provision proxy services, and handle your reseller operations.\n\nPerfect for:\n- White-label proxy reselling\n- Automated customer provisioning\n- Integration with your billing system\n- Custom control panels\n\n## Development/Sandbox Environment\n**Test your integration without affecting real data or completing KYC!**\n\nUse our development API at: `https://dashboard.proxyomega.com/api/reseller/v1/dev`\n\nFeatures:\n- **No authentication required** - No API key needed\n- **No KYC required** - Test before completing identity verification\n- **Mock data responses** - Realistic test data\n- **No charges** - Balance remains unchanged\n- **Error simulation** - Add `?error=insufficient_balance` to test error handling\n- **Delay simulation** - Add `?delay=2` to test timeouts\n\n```bash\n# Test without authentication\ncurl https://dashboard.proxyomega.com/api/reseller/v1/dev/balance\n\n# Simulate an error\ncurl https://dashboard.proxyomega.com/api/reseller/v1/dev/balance?error=insufficient_balance\n```\n\n## Authentication & KYC Requirements\n**Production API** - Requires TWO things:\n1. **API Key** - Sent in `X-API-Key` header (found in Reseller Center > Overview)\n2. **KYC Verification** - Identity verification must be completed and verified\n\n```bash\ncurl -H \"X-API-Key: your_api_key_here\" \\\n  https://dashboard.proxyomega.com/api/reseller/v1/balance\n```\n\n### KYC Verification Status\n- \u2705 **KYC Verified** \u2192 Full access to production API\n- \u274c **No KYC / Pending** \u2192 Can only use development API at `/dev`\n\nComplete KYC verification in Reseller Center before accessing production API.\n\n## Rate Limits\n**Production API only**\n- **100 requests per minute** - Burst allowance\n- **1,000 requests per hour** - Sustained usage\n\nExceeding rate limits returns HTTP 429 with a `Retry-After` header.\n\nDevelopment API has no rate limits.\n\n## Wholesale Pricing\nYour wholesale prices are based on your reseller tier:\n- **Bronze**: 15% discount (default)\n- **Silver**: 20% discount ($5,000/month spending)\n- **Gold**: 25% discount ($10,000/month spending)\n- **Platinum**: 30% discount ($25,000/month spending)\n\n## Geographic Targeting\n\nAll proxy types support geographic targeting, but the method varies by product:\n\n### Platinum Residential & Mobile (Traffic-Based)\nTargeting is applied at **connection time** via username format parameters:\n\n| Parameter | Description | Format | Example |\n|-----------|-------------|--------|---------|\n| `country` | ISO 2-letter country code | lowercase | `country-us` |\n| `region` | State/region name | lowercase, spaces\u2192underscores | `region-california` |\n| `city` | City name | lowercase | `city-los_angeles` |\n| `asn` | ASN number | numeric | `asn-12345` |\n| `session` | Sticky session ID | alphanumeric | `session-abc123` |\n| `ttl` | Session duration in minutes | numeric | `ttl-30` |\n\n**Username Format:** `{username}-country-{code}-region-{state}-city-{city}-session-{id}-ttl-{minutes}`\n\n**Example:** `res_123_user1-country-us-region-california-city-los_angeles-session-abc123-ttl-30`\n\n**150+ countries available** including: US, GB, CA, DE, FR, IT, ES, NL, AU, JP, BR, IN, MX, KR, and more.\n\n### IPv6 Datacenter (Subscription-Based)\nTargeting via username format:\n- `country` - ISO 2-letter code (lowercase)\n- `session` - Sticky session ID\n- `ttl` - Session duration in minutes\n\n**108 countries supported.**\n\n### Unlimited Residential (Subscription-Based)\nUses **per-port configuration system** via the port-configs API endpoints:\n\n| Parameter | Description | Values |\n|-----------|-------------|--------|\n| `port_number` | Specific port (10000-100XX) | Based on subscription ports |\n| `rotation_minutes` | IP rotation interval | 1, 3, 5, 10, 15, 20, 30, 45, 60 |\n| `country_targeting` | Country code | 150+ countries |\n| `notes` | Optional description | Any text |\n\n**Key Difference:** Targeting is set via port configuration API, NOT via username format.\n\nUse `GET /sub-accounts/{id}/subscriptions/{subscription_id}/port-configs` to manage configurations.\n\n### Using the Proxy List Endpoint\nThe `/sub-accounts/{id}/proxy-list` endpoint generates formatted proxy lists with targeting applied:\n\n```bash\n# Generate 10 US proxies for platinum\ncurl -H \"X-API-Key: your_key\" \\\n  \"https://dashboard.proxyomega.com/api/reseller/v1/sub-accounts/123/proxy-list?product_type=platinum&country=us&quantity=10\"\n```\n\n## Error Handling\nThe API uses standard HTTP status codes:\n- `200` - Success\n- `400` - Bad Request (invalid parameters)\n- `401` - Unauthorized (invalid API key)\n- `403` - Forbidden (KYC not verified, insufficient balance, account suspended)\n- `404` - Not Found\n- `500` - Server Error\n\n### Common Error Examples\n\n**KYC Not Verified:**\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"error\": \"KYC verification required. Production API access requires verified identity. Use development API at /api/reseller/v1/dev for testing without KYC.\"\n}\n```\n\n**Insufficient Balance:**\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"error\": \"Insufficient balance. Required: $119.99, Available: $50.00\"\n}\n```",
    "contact": {
      "name": "ProxyOmega Support",
      "email": "support@proxyomega.com",
      "url": "https://dashboard.proxyomega.com"
    },
    "x-jentic-source-url": "https://api.swaggerhub.com/apis/proxyomegaltd/proxyomega-reseller-api-v1/1.0.0"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://dashboard.proxyomega.com/api/reseller/v1",
      "description": "Production API"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://dashboard.proxyomega.com/api/reseller/v1/dev",
      "description": "Development/Sandbox API (No authentication required, returns mock data)"
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "apiKey": []
    },
    {}
  ],
